{
  "name": "Client Onboarding Orchestrator",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🎯 CLIENT ONBOARDING ORCHESTRATOR\n**What it does:** New client webhook → creates a Notion project page, a Google Drive folder, and a Slack channel → posts a welcome message → sends the client a welcome email → schedules a kickoff call → logs every stage to Google Sheets → sends you a Telegram summary. Any failed step alerts the owner in Slack and marks the row `FAILED`.\n\n**You'll need:**\n- Notion integration + a client projects database (notion.so → My integrations)\n- Google Drive + Google Calendar + Gmail + Google Sheets OAuth2 credentials\n- Slack app with `channels:write` + `chat:write` scopes\n- Google Sheet with a `Clients` tab\n- Telegram bot token + your chat ID\n\n**Status flow in Sheets:** `RECEIVED` → `PROVISIONED` → `WELCOMED` (or `FAILED`)",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 3860,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "b25e7e47-8b20-40f0-82b1-5728d7655ae2",
      "name": "STICKY — Title",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 1 — Webhook intake + log RECEIVED\nPOST /new-client webhook (JSON: name, email, company) → CONFIG — Business → slugify the company name → append a row to the `Clients` tab with status `RECEIVED`.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 1160,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "74d7f2c8-28be-4e1f-a2d0-a966dc857917",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 2 — Provision the client workspace\nNotion project page in your database → Google Drive folder under your parent folder → Slack channel (`client-<slug>`) → welcome post in the channel tagging the owner. Each provisioning node continues on error: any failure jumps to the STEP 4 alert chain.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 980,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "dc911fff-4566-409a-85f7-b6bbdea2c32b",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        940,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 3 — Welcome email + kickoff → WELCOMED\nSheet flips to `PROVISIONED` → Gmail welcome email to the client → compute the kickoff date (N days out, 10:00, 45 min) → Google Calendar event with the client invited → sheet flips to `WELCOMED`.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 1180,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "5cb3b699-f28c-4e15-8759-e3d59082bd3b",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1940,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 4 — Failure alerts + Telegram summary\nAny failed step (Notion / Drive / Slack channel / Gmail / Calendar) posts an alert in Slack with the client + error → sheet flips to `FAILED`. On the happy path, Telegram sends the 🎉 client-onboarded summary with all the links.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 2560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "7600250d-2700-47b0-b244-260042919497",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        900,
        600
      ]
    },
